<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanthirava Narasaraja I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1615">1615</a>–<a href="/years/1659">1659</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanthirava Narasaraja I (1615–1659) was the Wodeyar king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> from 1638 to 1659. He defended his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> against forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a> and extended the kingdom at the expense of neighbouring chiefs, making Mysore a significant regional power after the fall of Vijayanagara. He is credited with setting up a royal mint and issuing coins in his own name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanthirava-narasaraja-i.jpg" alt="Kanthirava Narasaraja I" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (both photographer and original artist) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanthirava.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
